The function `next_bigger` finds the next higher number by rearranging the digits of the input number. It uses an efficient algorithm to ensure the solution is optimal and handles edge cases.

```python
def next_bigger(num: int) -> int:
    digits = list(str(num))
    n = len(digits)
    pivot = -1
    for i in range(n-2, -1, -1):
        if digits[i] < digits[i+1]:
            pivot = i
            break
    if pivot == -1:
        return -1
    for j in range(n-1, pivot, -1):
        if digits[j] > digits[pivot]:
            break
    digits[pivot], digits[j] = digits[j], digits[pivot]
    digits[pivot+1:] = reversed(digits[pivot+1:])
    result = int(''.join(digits))
    return result if result > num else -1
